peror_Wu_of_Han"}},{"id":"sima-qian","name":{"en":"Sima Qian"},"role":{"en":"Chinese historian"},"born":-145,"died":-86,"approx":true,"lat":34.27,"lng":108.92,"place":{"en":"Chang'an"},"region":"asia","category":"culture","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"The 'Father of Chinese history', author of the Records of the Grand Historian spanning two millennia."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Si%20maqian.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sima_Qian"}},{"id":"mithridates-vi","name":{"en":"Mithridates VI Eupator"},"role":{"en":"king of Pontus, enemy of Rome"},"born":-135,"died":-63,"approx":true,"lat":42.03,"lng":35.15,"place":{"en":"Sinope (Pontus)"},"region":"middle-east","category":"war","tier":3,"bio":{"en":"Fought Rome for nearly 25 years in three Mithridatic Wars; legend says he made himself immune to poisons."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mithridates%20VI%20Louvre.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mithridates_VI_Eupator"}},{"id":"cicero","name":{"en":"Cicero"},"role":{"en":"Roman orator and statesman"},"born":-106,"died":-43,"approx":false,"lat":41.89,"lng":12.48,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"culture","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Rome's greatest orator and master of Latin prose, who exposed Catiline's conspiracy; killed in the Second Triumvirate's proscriptions."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bust%20of%20Cicero%20(1st-cent.%20BC)%20-%20Palazzo%20Nuovo%20-%20Musei%20Capitolini%20-%20Rome%202016.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cicero"}},{"id":"pompey","name":{"en":"Pompey the Great"},"role":{"en":"Roman general and statesman"},"born":-106,"died":-48,"approx":false,"lat":41.9,"lng":12.47,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"war","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Conqueror of the East and member of the First Triumvirate; lost the civil war to Caesar and was murdered in Egypt."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pompey%20the%20Great.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompey"}},{"id":"spartacus","name":{"en":"Spartacus"},"role":{"en":"gladiator, leader of a slave revolt"},"born":-103,"died":-71,"approx":true,"lat":41.08,"lng":14.25,"place":{"en":"Capua"},"region":"europe","category":"war","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Thracian gladiator who led the largest slave uprising in Italy and defeated several Roman armies."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%CE%A3%CF%80%CE%AC%CF%81%CF%84%CE%B1%CE%BA%CE%BF%CF%82%20Spartacus%2CEspartaco%20marble%20statue%20in%20Louvre%20%22%CE%9C%CE%B1%CE%B9%CE%B4%CE%BF%CE%B9%20clan%20-Meadow%22%20slave%20macedon-greek.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spartacus"}},{"id":"julius-caesar","name":{"en":"Julius Caesar"},"role":{"en":"Roman general and dictator"},"born":-100,"died":-44,"approx":false,"lat":41.89,"lng":12.48,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"politics","tier":1,"bio":{"en":"Conquered Gaul, crossed the Rubicon and became dictator for life; assassinated on the Ides of March."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Retrato%20de%20Julio%20C%C3%A9sar%20(26724093101)%20(cropped).jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julius_Caesar"}},{"id":"herod-the-great","name":{"en":"Herod the Great"},"role":{"en":"king of Judea"},"born":-72,"died":-4,"approx":true,"lat":31.78,"lng":35.23,"place":{"en":"Jerusalem"},"region":"middle-east","category":"politics","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Roman client king of Judea who rebuilt the Temple and built Masada and Caesarea; the Gospels blame him for the Massacre of the Innocents."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/HerodtheGreat2.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herod_the_Great"}},{"id":"virgil","name":{"en":"Virgil"},"role":{"en":"Roman poet"},"born":-70,"died":-19,"approx":false,"lat":41.9,"lng":12.49,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"culture","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Rome's greatest poet, author of the Aeneid, the national epic of the Trojan Aeneas, ancestor of the Romans."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Parco%20della%20Grotta%20di%20Posillipo5%20(crop).jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virgil"}},{"id":"cleopatra","name":{"en":"Cleopatra"},"role":{"en":"last queen of Ptolemaic Egypt"},"born":-69,"died":-30,"approx":false,"lat":31.2,"lng":29.92,"place":{"en":"Alexandria"},"region":"africa","category":"politics","tier":1,"bio":{"en":"Last ruler of the Ptolemaic dynasty, ally of Caesar and Mark Antony; she took her own life after defeat at Actium."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Kleopatra-VII.-Altes-Museum-Berlin1.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra"}},{"id":"augustus","name":{"en":"Augustus"},"role":{"en":"first Roman emperor"},"born":-63,"died":14,"approx":false,"lat":41.89,"lng":12.49,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"politics","tier":1,"bio":{"en":"Caesar's adopted heir who defeated Antony and Cleopatra and founded the Roman Empire, ushering in the Pax Romana."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Statue%20of%20the%20Emperor%20Octavian%20Augustus%20as%20Jupiter%20(6).png?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus"}},{"id":"amanirenas","name":{"en":"Amanirenas"},"role":{"en":"queen (kandake) of Kush"},"born":-60,"died":-10,"approx":true,"lat":16.94,"lng":33.75,"place":{"en":"Meroë"},"region":"africa","category":"war","tier":3,"bio":{"en":"One-eyed kandake of Meroë who fought Rome in the 20s BC and won a favourable peace from Augustus."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Stele%20hamadab.JPG?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amanirenas"}},{"id":"livia","name":{"en":"Livia Drusilla"},"role":{"en":"wife of Augustus, first Roman empress"},"born":-59,"died":29,"approx":false,"lat":41.89,"lng":12.49,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"politics","tier":3,"bio":{"en":"Wife and adviser of Augustus and mother of Emperor Tiberius, one of the most powerful women in Roman history."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Antica%20roma%2C%20testa%20di%20livia%2C%20in%20marmo%2C%20da%20fayoum%2C%20copia%20del%20I%20secolo%20dc%20di%20un%20originale%20del%2027-23%20ac%20ca.%2C%20IN%201444.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livia"}},{"id":"seneca-the-younger","name":{"en":"Seneca the Younger"},"role":{"en":"Roman Stoic philosopher"},"born":-4,"died":65,"approx":true,"lat":41.89,"lng":12.49,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"culture","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Stoic whose Moral Letters to Lucilius teach calm acceptance of fate and the value of time. Tutor and adviser to Nero, on whose orders he took his own life."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Duble%20herma%20of%20Socrates%20and%20Seneca%20Antikensammlung%20Berlin%2007.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seneca_the_Younger"},"schools":["stoicism"]}]